      "monotonicity_test_passed": true,
      "technical_explanation": "In the legacy 12-feature unconstrained HGB model, tree splits on quali_gap_pct (+5.18%) and grid_pos (P21) interacted non-monotonically with driver_form_3 (1.67), causing P21 to receive a HIGHER podium probability (36.06% raw / 40.24% calibrated) than starting P11 (25.12% raw). Enforcing monotonic_cst (-1 on Qualifying_Rank and Starting_Grid_Position) eliminates all positive jumps across P1..P22 (0 violations out of 924 transitions). Furthermore, as noted in Phase 1.2, holding Verstappen's elite Driver_Form (1.67), Driver_Track_History at Interlagos, and Delta_Q_to_G (+5 penalty indicator) constant, the monotonic HGB curve decreases from P1 (74.6%) down to a flat right-leaf plateau from P7..P21 (29.27% raw / 26.98% calibrated), whereas listwise Plackett-Luce gives P_Podium_PL = 1.98% and LogisticRegression gives P_Podium_LR = 1.24%."
